00:27:12.830 --> 00:27:16.960
white flag. The leaders enter the last lap in a dead heat.

00:27:39.440 --> 00:27:47.200
Weatherly, a lap behind at number 48, Petty in 42, and Beauchamp in 73, the leader, one

00:27:47.200 --> 00:27:47.940
mile to go.

00:27:55.270 --> 00:27:55.850
Final stretch.

00:27:56.590 --> 00:27:59.410
Weatherly is high on the track, Lee Petty in the center.

00:28:00.030 --> 00:28:01.010
Beauchamp below him.

00:28:06.680 --> 00:28:08.580
Flag, the race is over.

00:28:09.190 --> 00:28:12.370
Both Petty and Beauchamp clock in the identical time.

00:28:12.960 --> 00:28:15.440
3 hours, 41 minutes, 22 seconds.

00:28:16.700 --> 00:28:18.960
Beauchamp and Petty both wheel to the winner's circle.

00:28:19.850 --> 00:28:21.970
Both accept congratulations of the crowd

00:28:21.970 --> 00:28:24.910
in one of the most amazing finishes ever recorded

00:28:24.910 --> 00:28:26.270
in stock car racing.

00:28:27.590 --> 00:28:29.690
The on-the-spot, unofficial decision.

00:28:30.120 --> 00:28:33.220
went to Johnny Beauchamp, pending examination of photos.

00:28:36.040 --> 00:28:41.340
Both cars posted a speed of 135.52 miles an hour,

00:28:42.380 --> 00:28:46.340
34 miles an hour faster than any race ever run

00:28:46.340 --> 00:28:49.080
by an American stock passenger automobile.

00:28:53.290 --> 00:28:55.950
Official decision, based on photos such as this,

00:28:56.360 --> 00:28:59.960
gave Lee Petty in number 42 the victory by a margin...

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:03.800
of less than one yard over Johnny Beauchamp's number 73.

00:29:04.690 --> 00:29:09.050
Joe Weatherly, in number 48, a lap behind, took fifth place.

00:29:10.100 --> 00:29:15.060
After 500 miles, Lee Petty's margin of victory was one yard.

00:29:15.860 --> 00:29:19.300
Besides driving a great race, Petty was mechanic

00:29:19.300 --> 00:29:20.560
for his winning Oldmobile.

00:29:21.640 --> 00:29:25.600
Lee Petty becomes the winner of the first 500-mile event

00:29:25.690 --> 00:29:28.090
on Daytona's International Speedway.

00:29:30.190 --> 00:29:39.610
the test is over the crowds are gone the great launching sites wait for another year in the

00:29:39.610 --> 00:29:48.490
garages mechanics uncover the secrets of success and failure while the moon sends down a silent

00:29:48.490 --> 00:29:58.810
challenge in the missiles created here man has dared to ride into the unknown the same daring

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:01.900
will carry him into outer space.

00:30:18.080 --> 00:30:20.680
Because men have always ventured into the unknown,

00:30:21.960 --> 00:30:24.440
the moon which lights the empty racetracks

00:30:24.440 --> 00:30:28.100
may soon become mankind's first pit stop.

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:33.890
fueling station in the race to the stars.
